2a:["$","div","How to shortlist and compare schools",{"className":"space-y-3","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-display text-lg font-semibold","children":"How to shortlist and compare schools"}],[["$","p","Start with distance and commute time, because a ",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground md:text-base","children":"Start with distance and commute time, because a long daily journey tires young children. Then compare board affiliation (CBSE, ICSE, state board or IB), medium of instruction, class sizes, fee structure, transport availability and facilities such as labs, sports grounds and libraries."}],["$","p","Visit the school if possible. Meet the staff, se",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground md:text-base","children":"Visit the school if possible. Meet the staff, see the classrooms and ask about teacher qualifications, safety measures and how parent communication works. A visit tells you more than a brochure."}]],["$","ul",null,{"className":"list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5 text-sm text-muted-foreground","children":[["$","li","Check the board affiliation number on the board’s official site",{"children":"Check the board affiliation number on the board’s official site"}],["$","li","Ask for the full fee breakup, including annual charges and transport",{"children":"Ask for the full fee breakup, including annual charges and transport"}],["$","li","Check admission dates and age cut-offs early; they vary by state and school",{"children":"Check admission dates and age cut-offs early; they vary by state and school"}]]}],null]}]
2b:["$","div","Admissions, age limits and the RTE Act",{"className":"space-y-3","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-display text-lg font-semibold","children":"Admissions, age limits and the RTE Act"}],[["$","p","Many schools fix a minimum age for entry, such a",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground md:text-base","children":"Many schools fix a minimum age for entry, such as 3 years for nursery or 5 to 6 years for Class 1 as on a cut-off date. Use our age calculator to check your child’s age on the date the school specifies. Under the Right to Education Act, private unaided schools are required to reserve a share of seats for children from economically weaker sections; the process is run by the state, so check your state’s RTE portal for dates."}]],null,null]}]
